From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 09:54:16 +0000
Subject: net: ethernet: lantiq: release the DMA channel when hdma_port_enable
 fails

hdma_port_enable() had no rollback. Every failure exit after
ltq_request_dma() had already succeeded returned with the channel still
marked CHAN_IN_USE and the per-port armed bit still clear, so the retry
the CBM probe tail promises - "ndo_open will retry" - was impossible:
ndo_open step 1 calls in again, ltq_request_dma returns -EBUSY, and
ndo_open's unwind runs only the TMU undo for a step-1 failure, never
hdma_port_disable. The port could not come up again for the rest of the
boot.

This was inert while only dequeue port 10 was served and its probe-time
open had always succeeded. Now that all four LAN ports are armed at the
CBM probe tail it is four times the exposure, and the failure mode - one
silently dead LAN port, with only a dev_warn at probe to show for it -
is exactly the kind that costs a hardware iteration to diagnose.

Route the six post-request failure exits through an err_release label that
closes, frees the descriptor slot and releases every channel the call
acquired, so a failure leaves the port as it was found. Releasing only
entries [0, i] is deliberate: later table entries were never requested.
Both ltq_free_dma() (clears CHAN_IN_USE) and ltq_dma_chan_desc_free()
(idempotent with no ring) are safe on a channel that got no further than
ltq_request_dma, and dma_chan_close() on a never-opened channel just clears
an already-clear ON bit.

Also correct hdma_port_disable's claim that its unarmed-port path is the
ndo_open rollback. It is belt-and-braces, not load-bearing: enable now
cleans up after itself, and ndo_open does not call disable for a step-1
failure in any case.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/dma/hdma.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/dma/hdma.c
index f45b9fd476d2..ed19a318ae5c 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/dma/hdma.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/dma/hdma.c
@@ -2333,7 +2333,7 @@ int hdma_port_enable(int port_id)
 			if (ret) {
 				pr_err("hdma_port_enable(%d): init_cbm_dqm_dma_port(%d) failed: %d\n",
 				       port_id, e->cbm_deq, ret);
-				return ret;
+				goto err_release;
 			}
 
 			ret = ltq_dma_chan_desc_cfg(chan,
@@ -2342,7 +2342,7 @@ int hdma_port_enable(int port_id)
 			if (ret) {
 				pr_err("hdma_port_enable(%d): ltq_dma_chan_desc_cfg(%s, DQM-window) failed: %d\n",
 				       port_id, e->label, ret);
-				return ret;
+				goto err_release;
 			}
 			pr_info("hdma_port_enable(%d): %s CBM-managed, desc@phys 0x%08x x%u\n",
 				port_id, e->label,
@@ -2355,20 +2355,21 @@ int hdma_port_enable(int port_id)
 		if (ret) {
 			pr_err("hdma_port_enable(%d): ltq_dma_chan_desc_alloc(%s) failed: %d\n",
 			       port_id, e->label, ret);
-			return ret;
+			goto err_release;
 		}
 		pch = dma_chan_l2p(chan);
 		if (!pch) {
 			pr_err("hdma_port_enable(%d): dma_chan_l2p(%s) returned NULL\n",
 			       port_id, e->label);
-			return -EINVAL;
+			ret = -EINVAL;
+			goto err_release;
 		}
 		ret = ltq_dma_chan_desc_cfg(chan, pch->desc_phys,
 					    HDMA_PORT_DESC_NUM);
 		if (ret) {
 			pr_err("hdma_port_enable(%d): ltq_dma_chan_desc_cfg(%s) failed: %d\n",
 			       port_id, e->label, ret);
-			return ret;
+			goto err_release;
 		}
 chan_on:
 		ltq_dma_chan_irq_disable(chan);
@@ -2376,7 +2377,7 @@ int hdma_port_enable(int port_id)
 		if (ret) {
 			pr_err("hdma_port_enable(%d): ltq_dma_chan_open(%s) failed: %d\n",
 			       port_id, e->label, ret);
-			return ret;
+			goto err_release;
 		}
 		pr_info("hdma_port_enable(%d): opened %s (cid=%u pid=%u nid=%u)\n",
 			port_id, e->label, e->cid, e->pid, e->nid);
@@ -2384,6 +2385,20 @@ int hdma_port_enable(int port_id)
 
 	hdma_deq_set_armed(port_id);
 	return 0;
+
+err_release:
+	while (1) {
+		const struct port7_chan_desc *e = &tbl[i];
+		u32 c = _DMA_C(e->cid, e->pid, e->nid);
+
+		ltq_dma_chan_close(c);
+		ltq_dma_chan_desc_free(c);
+		ltq_free_dma(c);
+		if (i == 0)
+			break;
+		i--;
+	}
+	return ret;
 }
 
